## Morton / Hilbert dispatch ordering

Space-filling curve ordering for dispatch interleaving. Same
constraint representation as greedy grouping. Deferred per
not day-one.

## Wider-W bin_pack variant

`bin_pack` ships with a `Cap` up to 64-ish items per bin (bounded
by internal `Mask<Bits<64, Hot, Unsigned>>` helpers where consumers
pair it with hierarchical co-firing flags). Instantiating the same
helpers with `W = Bits<256, Hot, Unsigned>` would support >64 flags
per group via WideBits storage without an
algorithmic-shape change. Common pipeline workloads in observed
research stay well under 64 flags, so this is a non-urgent
widening.

- Carry greedy_group's fresh-accumulator requirement as a property
 rather than as prose plus a guard. The function documents that a
 well-formed predicate always accepts the first item of a fresh
 group, and pays for the cases where it does not with an extra
 predicate call and a branch on every group-open, present so the walk
 cannot loop forever. That requirement is exactly what a typed
 predicate can carry: under the unified predicate of round
 202607290200 the property rides on the predicate type, and the guard
 is selected away for any predicate that promises it while remaining
 for any that cannot. This is the one property in arvo with a named
 consequence in shipped source, so it is the first candidate when the
 property set gets populated. Blocked on the unified predicate.
